WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.291 --> 00:00:04.004
Well, well our war hero has arrived.

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:05.422
‘Killers of the Flower Moon’

00:00:05.422 --> 00:00:06.965
was a series of murders

00:00:06.965 --> 00:00:08.299
of Osage men and women,

00:00:08.299 --> 00:00:10.301
to bilk them after the discovery

00:00:10.301 --> 00:00:11.594
of oil on their land.

00:00:11.594 --> 00:00:13.054
The Osage reign of terror

00:00:13.054 --> 00:00:16.224
was a fascinating piece of American history.

00:00:16.224 --> 00:00:18.810
I was drawn to the idea to tell this terribly

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:19.602
tragic story that

00:00:19.602 --> 00:00:21.688
was never brought to national attention.

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:24.232
Marty’s obsessed with telling this story with

00:00:24.232 --> 00:00:26.401
the most honesty that he possibly could. 

00:00:26.401 --> 00:00:27.694
One of the key things,

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:28.695
was that I was drawn to this world

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:31.406
where friendship and love existed

00:00:31.406 --> 00:00:33.950
with blatant extortion, exploitation, and murder. 

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:37.162
When this money start coming,

00:00:37.162 --> 00:00:39.122
we should’ve known it came with something else.

00:00:40.123 --> 00:00:42.792
In our film, Ernest develops a relationship

00:00:42.792 --> 00:00:44.502
with Mollie Burkhardt. 

00:00:44.502 --> 00:00:45.920
I don’t know what you said,

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:48.131
but it must’ve been Indian for handsome devil.

00:00:48.131 --> 00:00:49.799
Ernest was encouraged to marry her

00:00:49.799 --> 00:00:51.134
by his uncle Bill Hale.

00:00:51.134 --> 00:00:52.260
In order to get her family

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:53.511
shares in the oil profits. 

00:00:53.511 --> 00:00:57.223
Hale was a very enigmatic presence in Osage country.

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:58.600
He definitely represented somebody

00:00:58.600 --> 00:00:59.684
that wanted to take advantage

00:00:59.684 --> 00:01:01.561
of the situation at all costs.  

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:02.896
Their time is over. 

00:01:03.772 --> 00:01:05.899
There was a need to tell this story

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:07.150
from Martin Scorsese.

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:08.568
There was something intrinsic

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:10.737
in him to do this story justice. 

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:11.863
There’s a sinister nature

00:01:11.863 --> 00:01:13.156
of the murders of the Osage people. 

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:16.451
Expecting a miracle to make this all go away?

00:01:16.451 --> 00:01:18.912
You know they don’t happen anymore. 

00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:21.122
I wanted to do justice to the Osage.

00:01:22.207 --> 00:01:23.541
So that the audience feels

00:01:23.541 --> 00:01:25.126
the immensity of the tragedy. 

